| `age_str`      | `age_string`        | whole-word is more readable                                             |
| `reader`       | `csv_reader`        | which kind of reader?                                                   |
| `out_dir`      | `output_dir`        | abbreviation; matches the parameter name                                |
| `valid_path`   | `valid_users_path`  | same pattern: "valid what?"                                             |
| `err_path`     | `error_report_path` | same as above                                                           |
| `summary_path` | `summary_file_path` | minor, but `path` alone is already implied by the type                  |
| `dry_run`      | —                   | good parameter name                                                     |
**Key pattern:** ambiguous plurals (`valid`, `errors`, `rows` need qualifiers), single-letter `i`, and abbreviations (`out_dir`, `errs`, `age_str`).

